From: retrorepair <joelwhybrow@googlemail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] HID: guncon2: report the full 16-bit Y

The GunCon 2's report is three little-endian 16-bit fields: buttons, X and Y. The driver
reads X as 16 bits but takes only the low byte of Y (data[4]), so every line past 255
wraps to 0, 1, 2... The gun counts lines since VSync, and a 15 kHz picture reaches line 257
to 273 on several MiSTer cores (Terminator 2, Point Blank 2, Time Crisis), so the bottom of
the screen reads as the top.

A raw capture of the endpoint with the gun aimed at a lit picture (tools/mister/usbraw.py)
shows data[5] is 0x01 in 143 of 1838 reports and 0x00 in all the others, as the high byte of
Y would be.

Not applied to any kernel by this repo: the MiSTer app works around it
(lightgun_crt.cpp, CRTGUN_Y_WRAP) until the driver is fixed, then that block can go.
---
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-guncon2.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-guncon2.c
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@
     if (urb->actual_length == 6) {
         /* Aiming */
         x = (data[3] << 8) | data[2];
-        y = data[4];
+        y = (data[5] << 8) | data[4];
 
         input_report_abs(guncon2->input_device, ABS_X, x);
         input_report_abs(guncon2->input_device, ABS_Y, y);
